      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that the sudden loss of a clear purpose feels like a massive void, making the idea of \"working through\" it seem impossible. That feeling of being an observer is a classic sign of deep emotional exhaustion, and it's far more than just \"going through the motions.\" While your past purpose is gone, this is a time to gently explore what might bring you even a tiny flicker of genuine interest or comfort right now. Please consider talking to a therapist who specializes in existential issues to help navigate this profound shift.",
      "source": "target",
